The paper supports a more faithful family than the initial “arbitrary cube sum” idea: Theorem 1.7 treats the full \(\mathrm{GL}\)-orbit of the divided-power Fermat cubic, and Lemma 1.6 makes a power-sum decomposition an exact certificate. I’m testing a Track B construction in that native orbit: a hidden Walsh–Hadamard change of variables gives a short structural route, while the standard contraction/matrix-pencil route requires dense exact linear algebra.
